{
  "_readme": [
    "Golden vectors pinning BOB's criticality scorer across its two implementations:",
    "  iOS    bob-ios/BOB/Sources/Sync/WorkItemScoring.swift        (BOBTests/ScoringVectorTests.swift)",
    "  server bob/functions/scoring.js                              (functions/scoring.test.js)",
    "",
    "The algorithm runs in both places because BOB must work fully offline. That is a",
    "deliberate duplication, and PORTING_CONTRACT 2.3 is the record of what it costs: four",
    "divergences that nobody noticed until someone read both listings side by side, plus a",
    "fifth found on 2026-07-28 \u2014 Firestore stores `theme` as BOTH an id (314 of 500 sampled",
    "stories) and a name (174), the server matched only names and iOS only ids, so for any",
    "themed item one engine added 10 and the other 0. Both now normalise first.",
    "",
    "As of 2026-07-28 both implementations pass all of these. Change a constant in either",
    "one and you change it in the other and here, in the same commit \u2014 otherwise one of the",
    "two builds goes red, which is the entire point.",
    "",
    "nowMs is pinned so results are deterministic. Expectations were produced by executing",
    "the real server function with Date.now stubbed, so they are the reference",
    "implementation's own output rather than a transcription of it.",
    "",
    "functions/scoringVectors.json is a vendored copy and must stay byte-identical."
